# Go build output
# Binaries and build artifacts. The bare repo name catches `go build` with no -o flag.
/atlassian-mcp-lite
/bin/
/dist/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out

# Go tooling
# `go test -coverprofile`, pprof output, and the workspace file (machine-local by design).
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.prof
*.pprof
go.work
go.work.sum

# Dependencies are resolved from the module cache, not vendored. If this project
# ever adopts `go mod vendor`, commit vendor/ rather than ignoring it — a vendored
# tree is part of the build.

# Docker Compose
# Compose files themselves are tracked; only machine-local overrides and state are not.
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yaml
compose.override.yml
compose.override.yaml
.docker/
docker/data/

# Environment and secrets
# .env holds the Atlassian site URL and API token; never commit it. The example file is tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!testdata/**/*.pem
!testdata/**/*.key

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs and local runtime
*.log
/tmp/
/var/

# Knowledge base integration
graphify-out
graphify-out/
docs/kb
.serena

CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
